 "notes": "Headline result: 2-sigma (95% CL) limit on DM two-body decay lifetime from XRISM/Resolve observation of the Centaurus cluster (285 ks), using the novel double-narrow-line (cluster + Milky Way) analysis (Fig.3 left panel). Recast into ALP-photon coupling in Fig.4 left panel (blue 'This work' region), which is the digitized source. x-axis m_phi[keV] is the ALP (DM particle) mass; converted to eV (x1000). Photon energy is m_phi/2. Convention: paper Eq.11 Gamma^-1=4.2e24 yr (1e18 GeV/g)^2 (keV/m)^3 with q=2 photons, equivalent to Gamma=g^2 m^3/(64 pi) with canonical g_agamma (L=-(g/4) a F Ftilde); verified numerically, so no conversion needed. Curve traced as the lower envelope (bottom edge, deepest reach per mass bin) of the very spiky blue excluded region via vector get_drawings; blue excludes g ABOVE the curve. Gray region in figure is XMM-Newton blank-sky (not this work) and is not traced. Gap near 13-13.6 keV is a masked line region. Limit is a decay search (flux ~ rho, linear); depends on the assumed NFW profiles (cluster rho_s=0.025 GeV/cm^3, r_s=0.33 Mpc; Milky Way rho_s=0.46 GeV/cm^3, r_s=0.0144 Mpc integrated over the FoV, Table 1) rather than a single local density, so dm_density_assumed set to null.",
